E2E harness for the staging re-run test plan (/home/philip/plan-staging-e2e-rerun.md, section 3).

Every harness workflow runs on push to trunk-merge/** and passes fast unless this run's control
file names its shape. A case PR adds exactly one file, e2e/active/<case-id>.json, in ONE commit.

The gate (.github/actions/e2e-gate) reads only the control files in the test branch tip's
first-parent diff (git diff --name-only HEAD^1 HEAD -- e2e/active/), so a predecessor's control
file is inert, and so are control files that land on main. Fallback: a top-level "pr": <N> field
limits a file to the test branch trunk-merge/pr-<N>/*.

Control file: {"<shape>": {<params>}, ...}. "fail_attempts" defaults to [1] wherever it exists.
  blocker    {max_min: 55}  waits for ref e2e-release/pr-<N>; exits 1 only if the ref ends -fail
  single     {fail_attempts, fail_sleep_s: {"<attempt>": s}, fail_attempts_b: [], sibling_sleep_s: 0,
              runs_on_attempt: {"<attempt>": "<runner label>"}}
  matrix     {fail_attempts}  leg 2 fails; e2e-rollup fails unless every leg passed
  two_a, two_b {fail_attempts, sibling_sleep_s: 0}
  reusable   {fail_attempts}  check run "e2e-call / e2e-called"
  status_a .. status_e {fail_attempts}  the spike's status shapes A-E (E posts from a called job)
  status_f   {}  dispatches e2e-status-f-poster.yml for this SHA
  g_build    {fail_attempts, report_delay_s: 5}  the workflow_run reporter posts e2e/g-own, e2e/g-trigger
  oddstatus  {fail: [cross_repo|cross_job|no_url|external|late|ext_check], late_s: 60}
  coe        {fail_attempts}  continue-on-error job
  conc       {fail_attempts, runs_on_attempt}  concurrency group e2e-conc-<test branch>
  dis        {fail_attempts}
  hang       {}  sleeps 50 minutes
Release a blocker: create refs/heads/e2e-release/pr-<N> (or ...-fail) at any commit.
